# Valgrind/memcheck suppressions for the cmux-tui leak sweep.
#
# The sweep exists to catch definite leaks (--leak-check=full
# --errors-for-leak-kinds=definite). Because it also runs with
# --error-exitcode=1, any ordinary memcheck error aborts the whole sweep,
# and the TLS-using test binaries (direct_wss_e2e, relay_wss_diagnostic)
# trip a well-known false positive before their leak summary is ever
# reached. Their leak summaries are clean: "definitely lost: 0 bytes in
# 0 blocks".
#
# Mechanism: ring's AES-GCM key schedule builds the expanded key and the
# GHASH tables in a stack MaybeUninit buffer that is filled by hand-written
# SIMD assembly (ring::aead::aes_gcm::Key::new). Memcheck cannot see those
# stores, so every byte derived from that key stays marked undefined. The
# taint then shows up in two places: a branch inside ring's own
# open_within, and the writev() that flushes the resulting rustls record
# to the socket. Both are reported with
# "Uninitialised value was created by a stack allocation
#     at ring::aead::aes_gcm::Key::new (aes_gcm.rs:44)".
#
# These entries are deliberately keyed on ring's AEAD frames and on
# rustls's record-flush frame so that uninitialised-memory reports from
# cmux code keep failing the sweep. The one accepted narrowing is that an
# uninitialised byte smuggled into a rustls record body would now be
# suppressed at the writev; there is no way to distinguish it from the
# ring-derived ciphertext in the same buffer.

{
   ring-aead-uninitialised-branch-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   ...
   fun:*ring*aead*
   ...
}

{
   ring-aead-uninitialised-branch-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   ...
   fun:*ring*aead*
   ...
}

{
   ring-aead-uninitialised-branch-value4
   Memcheck:Value4
   ...
   fun:*ring*aead*
   ...
}

{
   rustls-ring-record-flush-writev-0
   Memcheck:Param
   writev(vector[0])
   ...
   fun:*ChunkVecBuffer*write_to*
   ...
}

{
   rustls-ring-record-flush-writev-1
   Memcheck:Param
   writev(vector[1])
   ...
   fun:*ChunkVecBuffer*write_to*
   ...
}

{
   rustls-ring-record-flush-writev-2
   Memcheck:Param
   writev(vector[2])
   ...
   fun:*ChunkVecBuffer*write_to*
   ...
}

{
   rustls-ring-record-flush-writev-3
   Memcheck:Param
   writev(vector[3])
   ...
   fun:*ChunkVecBuffer*write_to*
   ...
}

{
   rustls-ring-record-flush-write-0
   Memcheck:Param
   write(buf)
   ...
   fun:*ChunkVecBuffer*write_to*
   ...
}
